  "Parts from step 1 are unchanged; they were correct.",
  "Circuit: Leonardo pin 2 -> blue wire -> button; button -> black wire -> GND. No resistor, since the sketch uses INPUT_PULLUP.",
  "The button straddles the breadboard centre gap at columns 4 and 6. In the image the half with rows f-j is the top half. I followed the catalogue naming, where rows f-j are bank 'b' and rows a-e are bank 't'.",
  "The button's two legs in column 4 (4b.f and 4t.e) are taken as side 1 and its two legs in column 6 (6b.f and 6t.e) as side 2. Pressing the button joins the two columns.",
  "The blue wire goes from pin 2 to column 6 (row i, so strip 6b). The black wire goes from GND to column 4 (row c, so strip 4t). Pressing the button therefore connects pin 2 to GND.",
  "The image highlights the GND pin next to 5V in the power header. I used GND.1 for it."
 ],
